A||||2||JohnnyK||Brake line frustration!!||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||12-18-2000||04:09 PM||||To anyone who has changed their rear brake line? HOw the heck do you do it? There is no way to bend it so that it connects up at the front to the splitter thingymadooey (2 lines go from the master cyl to the thingymadooey, where it is all split up). It's a larger line, and it's right in the bottom. Anyone had to do this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Brian||12-19-2000||06:43 AM||||Hi JohnnyK,<P>Long time, how'r ya doin?<P>I replaced all the lines in my 85GT project car.<BR>There are two seperate small dia. lines that come off the proportioning valve for the front wheels.<BR>A third, larger dia. line goes from the proportioning valve to a "T" block at the passenger rear wheel. From the "T" there's a smaller dia. line that runs to each of the two rear wheels.<BR>The two front & the passenger side rear lines can be purchased ready made, fittings & all just about anywhere. The main rear line & the branch that comes off the "T" & goes to the drivers rear wheel apparently have to be custom fabricated (cause they're so darn long). To complicate matters further these lines are metric & need a bubble flare (you've been there before&lt;g&gt; )<P>Hope that answers your question,<BR>Brian||||reg||6
Z||000002||JohnnyK||12-19-2000||11:20 AM||||Yeah, I'm letting my school work on it now. I had to take apart everything at the front thing (2 small front lines, etc) to fit the rear one under there, had the line fabricated with the old fittings and a coupler in the middle. Went to bleed it, and it started pissing out the coupler (it got stripped somehow)... Anyways, argh!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So how you doing?||||reg||1
